From 154a35ea226c9d7448532b11579a2098d9749c9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:34:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 84/85] hw/sensor: OPT3001 ambient light sensor and the Ambient
 2 Click

The OPT3001 (SBOS681C sections 7.3-7.6): result E[3:0] R[11:0] in
automatic or manual full-scale ranges with OVF and the exponent mask,
100 and 800 ms conversions in single-shot and continuous modes, CRF,
the low and high limits with fault counts in latched window and
transparent hysteresis modes, the end-of-conversion mode (low limit
exponent 11xxb, its reset value), the open-drain INT and its polarity,
and the ID registers. QOM "lux" (milli-lux) is the light.

Ambient 2 Click v100: 0x44 (ADDR on ground), INT on INT with R3
4.7 kOhm pull-up.

qtests: IDs, a conversion, the end-of-conversion INT, a latched high
fault, overflow and ME on the MC00's EXT1; the device ID through TWI0
on the AVR64EA48 Nano Base.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
